2186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347622 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347622 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186345779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347622 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0749705b-ee1b-5d79-b079-3b1d50ac9f5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347758 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347758 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347758 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347758 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347758 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347758 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347758 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347758 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186347297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347758 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5539bcfd-a712-5e1a-a393-3af3955fb0d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348410 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348410 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80540" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348410 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348410 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/50/506a298041a875549ec60c5cf99ebdbeb5ca4b5717037083fa6ca196fce27279.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If $R=[-2,2]\\times [0,3],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{2x+y}{y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. $\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+y}{y}, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin D\\end{aligned}$\n\nII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ \\frac{2x+y}{y}, & (x,y)\\in D∖R\\end{aligned}$\n\nIII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+y}{y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348410 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3b7813ca-41d9-58f5-aaf1-c07ba10ad235" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348410 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw our region $D$ and rectangle $R:$\n\n![](images/d2/d2b5c55b15f594680e8f299899d690cd1d92baa1ebef31ce5c79af52afec631e.png)\n\nNotice that the rectangle $R$ contains the region $D$ completely. \n\nNow, if we define $f(x,y)$ to be equal $\\frac{2x+y}{y}$ on $D$ and to be equal $0$ outside $D,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{2x+y}{y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given functions.\n\n- We cannot use function II. Since $D∖R$ is empty, the function $f(x,y)$ will be identical to zero for all points in $R,$ including $D.$ But $\\frac{2x+y}{y}$ is not zero, for example, at $(x,y)=(0,2)\\in D.$\n\n- Functions I and III equals $\\frac{2x+y}{y}$ on $D$ and equals $0$ outside $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351762 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351762 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351762 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "16080a41-2e2f-51fa-a9c4-12eb38603975" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352187 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352187 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352187 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "43b1980b-e87f-5251-b68d-f7b2a5280848" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352591 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352591 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352591 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "74bad7f9-9b45-59d6-9532-f075ca6e95ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352672 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352672 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352672 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7dd2e348-e399-5345-96ea-c3ac2b25e252" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352772 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352772 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218